WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.256
CROSS JOIN intentionally creates every possible pair
between two row sets In

00:00:06.282 --> 00:00:11.614
this example we combine selected departments with
appointment slots If we have

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:17.527
two departments and three time slots we expect six
combinations Run

00:00:17.553 --> 00:00:21.159
the query and verify that each selected department
appears once for each

00:00:21.185 --> 00:00:26.956
slot CROSS JOIN is useful for generating scenario
grids schedules

00:00:27.087 --> 00:00:33.248
calendars test cases or completeness frameworks But
it must be used deliberately

00:00:34.971 --> 00:00:40.236
Unlike an ordinary join there is no ON condition
restricting matches That

00:00:40.263 --> 00:00:45.827
means result size can grow very quickly Before
running a cross join

00:00:45.853 --> 00:00:51.224
on large tables estimate the number of combinations
Multiply the left row

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:55.277
count by the right row count If one side has ten
thousand

00:00:55.303 --> 00:00:58.527
rows and the other has ten thousand rows the result
can reach

00:00:58.553 --> 00:01:01.711
one hundred million combinations before any later
filtering
